 "structural_change": "rt_j (Claude group-B4 10-14): the engine glue is the hardened hub tile hgi_topk_hub_rt_j (u_hub at (453.6, 587.52), centre channel); cluster glue = 3 face FIFOs (pin flops at the W/E pins, pins ranged to the channel band y 520-720 so every FIFO <-> hub hop is <= ~450 um) + reset relays; command registered-ready, scores / results credit links. rt_i gate (-169.6 / -139.7) showed glue smeared over the outline; rt_h/rt_i fixes carried. rt_i (Claude group-B4 10-14): the rt_h --cts gate (never routed) measured TT placement reg->reg -226 ps / in->reg -251 ps; classes (re-timed on the gate's 4_cts.odb): u_hub.core.k -> out_row / st / emitted / of -289 / -237 / -180 / -72 ps (the 12-b emitted != k compare in front of the root pop and every MERGE-exit / output-FIFO enable), st -> s_valid -126 (st == FILL decode into the wreg ingress), u_bo.pin_v -> active / c_valid / b_r -67..-38 (bfifo i_r = up && cnt + pin_v < 4 combinational into the wreg skid), g_rel en -> e0/e1 -63 (218 endpoints: fire was the load enable of 108 node data flops), rst_n port -> 11 relay RESETN across 1.3 mm -251. rt_i fixes each at the source, cycle-identical: (1) remaining count rem = k - emitted with REGISTERED rz (rem==0) / r1 (rem==1) flags, lr_q = (row+1 == m) registered, mrg_q = (st_n == MERGE); (2) fill_q = (st_n == FILL) registered from an explicit next-state st_n; (3) bfifo RIR=1 on u_bo: i_r is a register loaded with next-state occupancy (pop only picks); (4) merge node writes the free slot at wp whenever !pv (never read before the fire that fills it); (5) cluster reset: port -> one synchroniser at the pin (u_crp) -> 11-region relay. Benches: short 11 + full 16 cases PASS with CASE lines byte-identical to rt_h; BYP / CLR / REV / FIFO-head mutants FAIL. rt_h (Claude group-B r2/B3 10-14): rt_g routed TT -102.77 / FF -38.32 / DRC 0 with three logic-depth classes, each fixed at the source, cycle-identical (short bench CASE lines byte-identical to rt_g source): (1) out_ready -> u_bo head_d 13 levels: the bfifo next head is a 2:1 of two candidates formed from registered state only, o_r selects; (2) u_hub.core f1_c -> f2_gt 18 / f1_s -> f2_e 13 levels: lane keys (canon/mono/~index, NaN flag) formed in front of the F1 register from the boundary FIFO head and the cursor register, F1->F2 holds only the 53-b threshold compare; (3) relay g_rel en -> od 19 levels: the merge node head/spill pair (parent pop steering all 108 data loads) is a 2-entry pointer FIFO, data written once at wp, od a 2:1 by rp. Children (heap rt_b, lane rt_e) unchanged. Short exact PASS (11 cases), BYP/CLR/REV/FIFO-head mutants FAIL.",
